r spoken conversations in past.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Continuous Tense in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span> tense to talk about actions that are happening now.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To make questions in the <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span> tense, you need to follow this structure: <br/></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"> (Wh) + <strong>be + subject + verb</strong> in \u2013ing + (complement) ?</div> </br><br/> Look at the following examples: <span class=\"italic\"> <li><strong>Are you taking</strong> the programming course?  <li>What programming language <strong>are you using</strong>?  <li><strong>Are you using</strong> the correct Boolean operator?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How are you doing with the course on programming?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you still studying the Boolean logic?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Now, are we getting similar results if we use the OR operator?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "How to Express Operators in Different Languages", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are three Boolean operators: <span class=\"strong\">AND</span>, <span class=\"strong\">OR</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">NOT</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Depending on the programming language that you are using, you need to consider how the Boolean operators are written.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Language\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">AND\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">OR\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">NOT\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Mathematics\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> \u02c4\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> \u02c5\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> \u00ac\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> \u201cC\u201d or C++\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> &&\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> ||\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> SQL\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> AND\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> OR\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> NOT\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Pascal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> AND\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> OR\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> NOT\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Perl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> &\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> ||\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Java\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> &\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> ||\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Basic\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> AND\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> OR\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> NOT\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "comparison  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an analysis of two or more statements to find similarities or differences ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is common that Boolean expressions have comparison operators such as equality, greater than, less than, greater than or equal to, less than or equal to, and inequality. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "entire ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "complete", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When you check the combinations of the AND operator, this entire expression evaluates as TRUE.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "consider", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to think about something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For example, consider this question: \u201cAre there more than 20 people studying in the library, and are there more than 20 computers?\u201d", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "both ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "referring to two things or people that are mentioned before", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(pronoun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the case of using OR as the operator, it is necessary that both values are False to evaluate to False.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "substitute ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to replace something with something else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When we substitute those values, we have True AND True. If you check the combinations of the AND operator, this entire expression evaluates as TRUE. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "prove ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say that something is true or false after analysis or test", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: First, you need to remember that the operands are the statements that can be proven True or False, and that there are three Boolean operators: AND, OR, and NOT. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Do some further research about Boolean Logic.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes about key ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a brochure to explain how Boolean Logic works and why it is important for computer science.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use simple sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your brochure with a partner. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I do further research about Boolean Logic.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes about key ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a brochure.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use simple sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my brochure with a partner. ", "type": "text"}]}]}